    "answer": {
      "short": "A. The sale price is less than the cost price (9% less).",
      "worked": "Let the cost price be $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Sale price}&=x\\times1.3\\times0.7\\\\\\text{Sale price}&=0.91x\\end{align*}$$\nThe sale price is 91% of the cost price, so it is 9% less.\n\nCorrect answer: A.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
